        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/journal.rs#L927-L964",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e9a25c6fad09b30e85a28120bd0f328ed51c639d1873ca118176149728564f8c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a578520cfe0244fb9ca05a9572ee657b",
      "statement": "Crash recovery (recover_journal) snapshots the journal region, decodes and validates frames from tail to head stopping at the first invalid frame, replays collected ops against the live image, flushes replayed metadata, then resets the journal header to a clean state with head=0, tail=0, cleanly_unmounted=true.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/disk.rs#L2172-L2210",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9162d4dc33fe4c2bea392a31ebcd06990cd8b6eb777a8a3a086c929e61ec3261:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4c7e247e01a648678391408e356c7661",
      "statement": "Four DurabilityMode variants control persistence: Strict (sync WAL per tx, deferred in-place flush batched at 50% ring watermark), Lazy (no per-tx barrier, relies on OS writeback), RangeAsync (batched async msync of mutation ranges), LegacyWholeMmapAsync (whole-file async msync).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/disk.rs#L2960-L3010",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a304fbd2dedb8e887f2b5c5ccdedce340ef9424107da493db9d88a4613548908:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/disk.rs#L3180-L3195",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2bd2cfb8d433bad65e30652c5afe4942f0834fe96c9437be4eeeaac5d45605aa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d28c97f05e73409f8c98dbf5b7f0db74",
      "statement": "Under Strict durability, group commit batches multiple transactions: when is_strict_sync_deferred() is true, individual commits skip their final flush_range and a background drainer performs a unified flush() barrier before completing the batch, amortizing msync cost while preserving WAL-before-data ordering.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/disk.rs#L2930-L2960",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ec14ed991244d124364a8b83e86c6d7d083891cdcb9f790ba2b34c2ea26223a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_017c51d6cdfb41ca99a220ef2d141977",
      "statement": "JBD2-style deferred checkpointing: in Strict mode, in-place metadata stays in page cache after apply; checkpoint_journal flushes all in-place metadata, sets tail=head, and persists the header. This is safe because the WAL still contains every transaction since the last checkpoint and replay is idempotent.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/disk.rs#L3180-L3200",
